From ac7b519f528df79fc7f53aa79b043fb215d8008e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 13:47:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] phase 4: services architecture, philosophy, FAQ, remove
 Practice Notes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Major additions:
- New /services overview page listing all 6 categories
- New /services/[slug] dynamic detail pages (6 static routes generated)
- ServicesSection on homepage — 6 category tiles in two-column grid
- PhilosophyBlock on homepage — 'Built around your needs. Not a package.'
- FaqBlock on homepage — 4 questions (accordion, client component)
- ServiceCategoryCard for the /services overview
- lib/services.ts helper for slug lookups and posture mapping

Removals:
- app/practice-notes/ route deleted entirely
- Practice Notes removed from nav array
- Pricing figures on Approach (£12,500 / £48,000 / £3,200) removed —
  replaced with 'Fixed-fee, quoted after a call' language

Reframes:
- CapabilitiesSection now framed as 'engagement types' / 'How we work'
  rather than 'capabilities' / 'What we do'
- Capability descriptions updated to reference service categories
  (Application, Cloud, Infrastructure, SOC 2, ISO 27001) more directly
- Approach page closing links to /services (new tie-in block)
- Homepage section numbering aligned: 01 How we work → 02 What we cover
  → 03 Who we help → 04 How we work (philosophy) → 05 The practice
  → 06 Common questions

Copy changes from template:
- 'We believe cybersecurity works best as a partnership' →
  'Cybersecurity works best as a partnership. Every engagement runs
  that way.'
- Removed 'In a meaningful way.' trailing fragment
- CTA labels reworded: 'See what X covers →' pattern

Content:
- content/site.ts substantially extended:
  - services array (6 categories with items, methodology, postures)
  - philosophy block content
  - faq array (4 items)
  - slogan added: 'Find the gaps. Fix the risks. Stay secure.'
  - Practice Notes removed from nav; Services inserted between
    Approach and Work
  - typicalCategories field added to capabilities (links to service slugs)
- Security Operations & Detection deferred; noted in code comment for
  easy addition when ready to publish.
